{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.96,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U7", "H9"],
      "pins": ["U7.24", "H9.1"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "In the KiCad netlist, U7 pin 24 (OA1, a TMC2209 motor output) and H9 pin 1 are both connected to the GND net. The Nutrient-B stepper driver therefore has one coil output tied to ground, and the corresponding A+ coil net present for U5 and U6 is missing.",
      "expected": "The specification states that each TMC2209 drives a two-phase coil output to its JST-XH connector. U7 pin 24 (OA1) should connect to H9 pin 1 as the Nutrient-B A+ motor output, analogous to U5 pin 24 to H7 pin 1 and U6 pin 24 to H8 pin 1, not to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"H9\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"24\") (pinfunction \"OA1\") (pintype \"output\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "each drives a 2-phase coil output (`/A_xx+/-`, `/B_xx+/-`) to connectors H7/H8/H9"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The Nutrient-B peristaltic dosing pump coil A is incorrectly shorted/forced to ground. The driver cannot properly energize that coil, and driving OA1 high may create a shoot-through or overcurrent condition in the TMC2209.",
      "confidence": 0.96
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a clear connectivity anomaly: TMC2209 U7 motor output OA1 and connector H9 pin 1 are tied to GND instead of forming the Nutrient-B A+ coil net, unlike U5 and U6. Other discrepancies noted in the specification are either known limitations or spec interpretation and are not reported as anomalies."
}

